===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[device]] that [[show]]s the [[time]]; a [[timepiece]].
#:{{synonyms|en|timepiece|clock|watch}}
# A person who [[keep]]s [[record]]s of the [[hour]]s of [[attendance]] of [[employee]]s.
# {{lb|en|sports}} A person who records the time [[elapsed]] in a [[sporting]] [[event]].
#:{{synonyms|en|timer}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The group member who controls the rhythm of the music when a group of musicians play together.
#*{{quote-book|1=en|year=2011|author=Harris M. Berger|title=Metal, Rock, and Jazz: Perception and the Phenomenology of Musical Experience|publisher=Wesleyan University Press|isbn=9780819571823|page=152|text=There was no consensus among jazz musicians about who was the primary '''timekeeper''' in a jazz band; some said the drummers and others said the bassist.}}
# {{q|usually with adjective}} A person (or something controlled by a person) that is [[punctual]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=April|author=Warren Smith|title=The problems of train regulation - a study of operation at Trent|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=217|text=As it happens, the [[Leicester]]-[[Beeston]] train is quite a good '''timekeeper''' - it sometimes runs a few minutes early - [...].}}

